  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>C3.S1 — Powers of the T gate</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<div style="background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:5px solid #026573;border-radius:8px;padding:16px 22px;margin-bottom:14px;"><p style="color:#026573;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0;">C3.S1 — Clifford hierarchy by hand</p></div><p>Let \(T=\mathrm{diag}(1,e^{i\pi/4})\).</p><p>(a) Give the smallest positive integer \(k\) with \(T^{k}=Z\).</p><p>\(k=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p><p>(b) Give the phase \(\lambda\) (a complex number) such that \(T^{ {@m@} }=\mathrm{diag}(1,\lambda)\).</p><p>\(\lambda=\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) \(T^{k}=\mathrm{diag}(1,e^{ik\pi/4})\). We need \(e^{ik\pi/4}=-1=e^{i\pi}\), i.e. \(k\pi/4\equiv\pi \pmod{2\pi}\), whose smallest positive solution is \(k=4\).</p><p>So \(T^2=S\), \(T^4=Z\), \(T^8=I\): \(T\) generates a cyclic group of order 8, and \(S,Z\) are Clifford while \(T\) is not — \(T\) sits at level 3 of the Clifford hierarchy. This is exactly why fault-tolerant cost is measured in T-count.</p><p>(b) \(T^{ {@m@} }=\mathrm{diag}(1,e^{i {@m@} \pi/4})={@ta2@}\) in the second entry.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1000000</penalty>
